# Nightly backup via cron, 02:30 Africa/Cairo. Install with `crontab -e` as root
# (or the user that owns BACKUP_DIR and can run `docker exec`):
#
#   CRON_TZ=Africa/Cairo
#   30 2 * * * /opt/invitation-platform/platform/infra/backup/backup.sh >> /var/log/invitation-backup.log 2>&1
#
# Notes:
# - CRON_TZ is supported by Vixie/ISC cron (default on Ubuntu 24.04). Verify
#   with `man 5 crontab` if unsure; otherwise set the system timezone instead:
#   `timedatectl set-timezone Africa/Cairo` (harden.sh already does this).
# - Use the ABSOLUTE path to backup.sh wherever you checked out the repo.
# - backup.sh auto-sources ../.env.prod relative to itself; override with
#   INFRA_ENV_FILE=/path/to/.env.prod in the crontab line if needed:
#   30 2 * * * INFRA_ENV_FILE=/etc/invitation-platform.env /opt/.../backup.sh >> /var/log/invitation-backup.log 2>&1
# - Prefer the systemd timer (backup.timer.example) on this box: it logs to
#   the journal (`journalctl -u invitation-backup`) and retries on failure.
CRON_TZ=Africa/Cairo
30 2 * * * /opt/invitation-platform/platform/infra/backup/backup.sh >> /var/log/invitation-backup.log 2>&1
